<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25253" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jōsēph</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭōsēph</span></b> , m.
		indecl.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of the patriarch Jacob</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 36,
				2, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen. 30, 24
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The husband of Mary, the mother of Jesus</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt.
				1, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 1,
			272</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An inhabitant of Arimathea</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Juvenc. 4, 720</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt.
				27, 57</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
